Design a digital potentiometer circuit that allows adjustment of a wiper position based on control signals and data inputs. It uses an n-bit representation for the wiper position, where n defaults to 8 bits, and features a total resistance of 1000 ohms. The resistive value is dynamically calculated as a function of the wiper position, thereby modifying the output resistance based on selections made via the control signals. The wiper position is updated in response to both control inputs and data inputs, ensuring precise control over the resistance in a digital format.
module top_module(
