description:
Design a dual-edge triggered D flip-flop that captures input data on both edges of the clock signal. The first flip-flop samples the data (d) on the rising edge of the clock, while the second flip-flop captures the output of the first one on the falling edge, ultimately providing a stable output (q) that reflects the input data with minimal delay across clock cycles. This design enhances the responsiveness of the D flip-flop by effectively utilizing both rising and falling edges of the clock.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output q
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output q
);reg q1, q2;

// First D flip-flop captures data on rising edge of clock
always @(posedge clk) begin
    q1 <= d;
end

// Second D flip-flop captures output of first flip-flop on falling edge of clock
always @(negedge clk) begin
    q2 <= q1;
end

// Output of second flip-flop is the output of the module
assign q = q2;

endmodule

