description:
Design a constant current driver circuit that generates a voltage output based on control signals. The module takes n control bits as input and outputs m bits of voltage, determined by the fixed current (10 mA) flowing through a specified load resistance (100 ohms). The output voltage is calculated by multiplying the current with the control signal value, which enables selection of different output levels. This driver is useful for applications requiring precise voltage regulation based on digital control inputs.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] ctrl,
  output [m-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] ctrl,
  output [m-1:0] out
);parameter n = 2; // number of control signals
parameter m = 1; // number of output signals
parameter I = 10; // current magnitude in mA
parameter R = 100; // load resistance in ohms

reg [n-1:0] ctrl_reg;
reg [m-1:0] out_reg;
wire i_wire;
wire v_wire;

assign i_wire = I / R;
assign v_wire = i_wire * {ctrl_reg, 1'b1};

assign out = out_reg;

always @ (ctrl) begin
  ctrl_reg <= ctrl;
  out_reg <= v_wire * R;
end

endmodule

