description:
Design a circuit that performs a specific multiplication operation on a 32-bit input. The module takes a 32-bit input value, shifts it left by 2 bits to multiply it by 4, adds this result back to the original input to yield a value, then shifts this sum left by 11 bits (equivalent to multiplying by 2048). Finally, it adds the original input to this last result to produce the final 32-bit output. This circuit effectively implements a custom multiplication algorithm.
module top_module(
    i_data0,
    o_data0
);

