description:
Design a circuit that converts a one-hot encoded input signal into its corresponding binary representation. The module takes a one-hot input of a specified width (16 by default) and produces a binary output that indicates the position of the '1' in the one-hot input. The binary output width is determined by calculating the logarithm base 2 of the number of one-hot inputs minus one, effectively providing a compact representation of the active input in binary form.
module top_module(
    input [ONEHOT_WIDTH-1:0] onehot,
    output [BIN_WIDTH-1:0] bin
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [ONEHOT_WIDTH-1:0] onehot,
    output [BIN_WIDTH-1:0] bin
);parameter ONEHOT_WIDTH = 16;
parameter BIN_WIDTH = $clog2(ONEHOT_WIDTH-1);

genvar i,j;
generate
    for (j=0; j<BIN_WIDTH; j=j+1) begin : jl
        wire [ONEHOT_WIDTH-1:0] tmp_mask;
        for (i=0; i<ONEHOT_WIDTH; i=i+1) begin : il
            assign tmp_mask[i] = i == j;
        end
        assign bin[j] = |(tmp_mask & onehot);
    end
endgenerate

endmodule

